-- title:
--   Primitivity of g forces cyclic kernel for ψ
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic a prime $q'$ which is algebraic over $\mathbb{Z}/q'$, and let $X_1/\kappa$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve all of whose $\kappa$-points killed by $q'$ are trivial. Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ satisfy $a<0$, $b<0$ and, for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, the condition that every nonzero element of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a unit precisely when $q'\in v$. Let $\Lambda_1\subset\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans over $\mathbb{Q}$, is finitely generated, and is maximal among such orders, and let $\theta_1$ be an injective ring map from the subring of $\operatorname{End}(X_1(\kappa))$ generated by the rationally represented (or zero) homomorphisms $X_1\to X_1$ into $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, with image exactly $\Lambda_1$. Fix a unit $x$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$, an elliptic curve $W/\kappa$, a nonzero additive map $\chi:X_1(\kappa)\to W(\kappa)$ lying in the rational hom set, and a unit $d$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ such that $\theta_1$ carries $\{\rho\circ\chi:\rho\in\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathrm{rat}}(W,X_1)\}$ onto the image of $d\cdot I_x$ under quaternion conjugation, where $I_y$ denotes the submodule [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19) $\Lambda_1\,y$, i.e. the elements of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ whose image in the adelic tensor product lies in $y\cdot$[`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) $\Lambda_1$. Let $g$ be a unit of the adelic tensor product lying in [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) $\Lambda_1$, let $W'/\kappa$ be elliptic and let $\psi:W(\kappa)\to W'(\kappa)$ and $\psi':W'(\kappa)\to W(\kappa)$ be additive maps in the respective rational hom sets with $\psi'\circ\psi$ and $\psi\circ\psi'$ both equal to multiplication by $n=\#\ker\psi$. Assume $\theta_1$ carries $\{\rho\circ(\psi\circ\chi):\rho\in\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathrm{rat}}(W',X_1)\}$ onto the conjugate of $d\cdot I_{xg}$, and that $\ell^{-1}g\notin$[`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) $\Lambda_1$ for every prime $\ell$. Then $\ker\psi$ is a cyclic group.
--
--   This is the 'primitive implies cyclic' direction of the kernel-ideal dictionary in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting: a sublattice $I_{xg}\subseteq I_x$ that is contained in no $\ell I_x$ is realised by an isogeny whose kernel is cyclic. It is cited in the construction of level structures attached to ideles, [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_equiv_ofFiniteIdele_mul_isAddCyclic_forall_ker_eq_of_kernelIdealSet_comp_eq`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_equiv_ofFiniteIdele_mul_isAddCyclic_forall_ker_eq_of_kernelIdealSet_comp_eq).
